<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms 1996/97 sugar output down 3.0 pct.</title>
<headline>EU confirms 1996/97 sugar output down 3.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar production estimate for 1996/97 (July/June) has settled at three per cent down on 1995/96, an EU member state official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The latest balance sheet shows no change over the previous estimate,&quot; the official said after the latest revision was presented to the EU sugar management committee on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The carry-forward figure for non-quota &quot;C&quot; sugar into the 1997/98 market continues to be put at 917,000 tonnes, up from 890,000 forecast in January.</p>
<p>EU sugar production (million tonnes):</p>
<p>				    1996/97	   1995/96</p>
<p>			     latest     last</p>
<p>					    (March 6)</p>
<p>     Area (mln/ha)	2.020     2.023	 2.082</p>
<p>2.  White Sugar</p>
<p>     Yield (t/ha)	 8.18	8.17	  7.47</p>
<p> 3.  Beet output	 16.515    16.521	15.564</p>
<p>     Cane output	  0.275     0.275	 0.250</p>
<p>     Molasses output    0.047     0.041	 0.045</p>
<p>     Total output	16.837    16.837	15.859</p>
<p>4.  Carryover from</p>
<p>     previous season    0.685     0.685	 0.535</p>
<p>5.  Total supplies</p>
<p>     (3+4)		 17.522    17.522	16.394</p>
<p>6.  Of which</p>
<p>     &quot;A&quot; Quota	   11.717    11.717	11.722</p>
<p>     &quot;B&quot; Quota	    2.450     2.450	 2.406</p>
<p>     &quot;C&quot; Non-quota	3.355     3.555	 2.266</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>Carry forward</p>
<p>     to next season     0.917     0.917	  0.685</p>
<p>     Exports		2.438     2.438	  1.581</p>
<p> 7.  Consumption	 12.554    12.600	 12.588</p>
